---
import Layouts from "../layouts/layouts.astro";
---

<Layouts title="Projects | Mubashir Dawood" description="Selected projects by Mubashir Dawood, including an AI content detector, a Go-based notes CLI, and a social network analysis tool.">
    <section id="projects">
        <h1 class="section-title">Selected Projects</h1>
        <div class="grid projects-grid">
            <div class="card project-card" id="project-1">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>SA Simple Books</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">An AI-native accounting web app for South African accountants, from bank statement to VAT201.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>Lets an accountant run real client books: upload a bank statement (PDF or CSV, laid out like FNB, Absa, Capitec, Nedbank, Standard Bank or Investec), and each transaction is categorised by the client's own rules, then built-in SA rules, then an AI fallback.
                            Confirming a transaction posts a balanced double-entry journal through a shared VAT engine, which feeds the chart of accounts, general ledger, trial balance, invoicing and VAT201 returns.
                            Amounts never touch floating point, and anything sent to the AI is masked and schema-validated first.
                            <a href="https://simple-books-jyn9.onrender.com/login" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">Visit Site</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>SvelteKit, TypeScript (Full Stack)</li>
                            <li>Postgres, Drizzle ORM (Ledger)</li>
                            <li>pdf.js (Statement parsing)</li>
                            <li>LLM API (AI categorisation)</li>
                            <li>Clerk (Auth)</li>
                            <li>Docker, Render (Deployment)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-2">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>JASS 2025 Annual Report</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A microsite built for JASS's 2025 annual report.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>A microsite built for JASS (Just Associates), presenting their 2025 annual report as an interactive web experience.
                            <a href="https://justassociates.org/mc/ar/2025/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">Visit Site</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>HTML</li>
                            <li>CSS</li>
                            <li>Vanilla JavaScript</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-3">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>Tab Bridge</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A Firefox extension + local MCP daemon that lets Claude read the HTML, console logs, network requests, and screenshots of tabs you explicitly allow.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>Lets Claude Code (or Claude Desktop) read the HTML, console logs, network requests, and screenshots of specific Firefox tabs you explicitly allow, plus any tab on a trusted local dev server, without a manual click every time.
                            A local daemon binds to 127.0.0.1 only, everything is read-only, and console/network capture is off by default until opted in per-tab.
                            <a href="https://github.com/MubashirD04/Tab-bridge" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">GitHub</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>TypeScript (Extension & Daemon)</li>
                            <li>WebSocket (Token-authed transport)</li>
                            <li>MCP (Claude Code / Desktop integration)</li>
                            <li>Firefox WebExtensions API</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-4">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>Workout Dashboard</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A fitness tracking dashboard with rich data visualisations and an AI coach that reads your own training data.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>Tracks workouts, cardio, body metrics, nutrition and progress photos, and turns them into charts: volume over time, a consistency heatmap, an athlete radar and a macro breakdown.
                            An AI fitness coach uses RAG, vector searching your logged data and expert knowledge, to give personalised advice.
                            Admin, trainer and client roles let trainers invite and follow their clients, while progress photos stay private to the client.
                            <a href="https://github.com/MubashirD04/Workout_Dashboard" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">GitHub</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>React, Vite, Tailwind CSS (Frontend)</li>
                            <li>Recharts (Visualisations)</li>
                            <li>Convex (Database & Vector search)</li>
                            <li>LLM API (AI coach)</li>
                            <li>Clerk (Auth & Roles)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-5">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>AI Content Detector</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A web app designed to detect whether text is AI generated or not.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>The AI Content Detector (AI-CD) is a web application designed to help users determine whether a given text is likely to have been generated by an AI or written by a human. 
                            The application consists of a Flask-based backend API for AI content detection and a React-based frontend for user interaction.
                            <a href="https://github.com/meekaaeelBooley/AI-Content-Detector" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">GitHub</a>
                        </p>
                        </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Flask (Backend)</li>
                            <li>React, Node.js (Frontend)</li>
                            <li>REST APIs</li>
                            <li>Self-trained detector model (Pandas, Numpy, Google Colab)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-6">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>Notes CLI</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A fast Go CLI that takes a lecture transcript, and appends them to a JSON file grouped by course.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>Adresses the problem of taking notes from lectures, and transforms lecture transcripts into structured, detailed AI notes. Grouped by course, synced to Joplin, and searchable via a built-in AI Assistant.
                            <a href="https://github.com/MubashirD04/Note-Creator-CLI-Tool" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">GitHub</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Go (Core Logic)</li>
                            <li>Groq (AI Handler)</li>
                            <li>Joplin (Interpreter)</li>
                            <li>JSON (local storage)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card project-card" id="project-7">
                <div class="accordion-header">
                    <div class="accordion-title-row">
                        <h3>Social Network RAG</h3>
                        <span class="accordion-icon"></span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="accordion-desc">A tool that turns raw group chat exports into an interactive social graph, exposed via an API, MCP server, and web UI.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-content-wrapper">
                    <div class="case-study-content">
                        <div class="case-study-info">
                        <h4>Overview</h4>
                        <p>Turns raw group chat exports (WhatsApp, Telegram, Slack) into an interactive directed graph using local machine learning, with no external LLM API costs for the core analysis.
                            It identifies key influencers (PageRank), information brokers (betweenness centrality), and community clusters, and supports semantic search (RAG) over the full conversation history.
                            A conversation-linking layer also infers likely connections between unthreaded messages, kept visually distinct from confirmed replies so a guess never inflates anyone's influence score.
                            <a href="https://github.com/MubashirD04/Social-Network-RAG" target="_blank" style="color: var(--primary-color);">GitHub</a>
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="case-study-tech">
                        <h4>Tech Stack</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>FastAPI, Uvicorn (API)</li>
                            <li>NetworkX, YAKE (Graph & Topic Analysis)</li>
                            <li>fastembed / ONNX Runtime (Embeddings)</li>
                            <li>MCP (Anthropic SDK)</li>
                            <li>React, Vite (Web UI)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layouts>